{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract methylation pileup [-h] [-r REGION] [--context {cpg,all}] [--5hmc | --no-5hmc]\n                                     [--combine-strands | --no-combine-strands]\n                                     [--format {tsv,parquet}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -r, --region REGION   Region(s), 1-based and inclusive: chr20:10000000-11000000 or chr1,chr2\n                        (default: the whole genome)\n  --context {cpg,all}   cpg: CpG sites only; all: every cytosine (CHG/CHH too). Overrides\n                        methylation_context in config.toml (default: cpg).\n  --5hmc, --no-5hmc     Also report 5-hydroxymethylcytosine (Nanopore 5mCG_5hmCG models).\n                        Overrides methylation_5hmc in config.toml (default: 5mC only).\n  --combine-strands, --no-combine-strands\n                        Sum both strands of each CpG into one row on its C. Overrides\n                        methylation_combine_strands in config.toml (default: on for CpG).\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Summary table format: tsv, or parquet (needs pyarrow), which also writes\n                        the sites as <stem>.<context>.bedmethyl.parquet (default: tsv)\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract methylation pileup --input ont.bam\n  wgsextract methylation pileup --input ont.bam --format parquet\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>.<context>.bedmethyl.gz (+ .tbi) and <input\n  stem>.<context>.methylation.tsv; with --format parquet the summary is\n  .methylation.parquet and the calls are also in <input\n  stem>.<context>.bedmethyl.parquet.\n\nneeds:\n  modkit, samtools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools;\n  hours on a 30x genome.\n",
